{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 3060,
    "dDurationMs": 6050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Picture this: you are thrown into a dingy\nroom and told \"you can't leave until you have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9110,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "created the thinnest material known to man.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11700,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only that, it must also be the strongest,\nthe best thermal conductor and as good at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17600,
    "dDurationMs": 3339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "conducting electricity as copper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20939,
    "dDurationMs": 3951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know, it sounds hopeless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24890,
    "dDurationMs": 6700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But luckily, you know something about nanotechnology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31590,
    "dDurationMs": 8170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, really really tiny devices and materials\nthat are less than 100 nanometers in size."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39760,
    "dDurationMs": 5459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course I don't have to tell you a nanometer\nis a billionth of a meter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45219,
    "dDurationMs": 3721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's roughly the size of ten atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48940,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do you create something that tiny?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52520,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's time to embrace your inner MacGyver."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54790,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're gonna need a pencil, some scotch tape\nand a healthy dose of elbow grease."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60530,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A pencil contains not lead but graphite, which\nconsists of sheets of carbon in a hexagonal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67290,
    "dDurationMs": 1209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lattice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68499,
    "dDurationMs": 5281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you write, layers of graphite slide off\nthe tip of the pencil and stick to the paper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73780,
    "dDurationMs": 6009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Usually, many layers are stacked on top of\neach other but once in a while you get a single"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79789,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "layer of carbon atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81969,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is called \"graphene\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84689,
    "dDurationMs": 8790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2004, Andre Geim and Konstantin Novoselov\ncreated graphene using nothing but graphite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93479,
    "dDurationMs": 2011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and scotch tape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95490,
    "dDurationMs": 4909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They placed a graphite flake onto the tape,\nfolded it in two and then cleaved the flake"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100399,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in half."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101549,
    "dDurationMs": 5810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They repeated this procedure a number of times\nand then studied the resulting fragments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107359,
    "dDurationMs": 5841,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To their astonishment they found some of the\npieces were only a single atom thick."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113200,
    "dDurationMs": 3939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was particularly unexpected because it\nwas thought a single layer of graphite would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117139,
    "dDurationMs": 5241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not be chemically stable, especially at room\ntemperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122380,
    "dDurationMs": 5279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Graphene conducts electrons faster than any\nother substance at room temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127659,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is because of the extraordinarily high\nquality of the graphene lattice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132069,
    "dDurationMs": 5321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists are yet to find a single atom out\nof place in graphene."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137390,
    "dDurationMs": 5519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since the electrons aren't scattered by defects\nin the lattice, they go so fast that Einstein's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142909,
    "dDurationMs": 4371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relativity must be used to understand their\nmotion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147280,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this perfect lattice is created by the\nvery strong yet flexible bonds between carbon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152580,
    "dDurationMs": 6620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "atoms -- making the substance bendable but\nharder than diamond."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159200,
    "dDurationMs": 6190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Graphene in incredibly strong -- if you could\nbalance an elephant on a pencil and support"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165390,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the pencil on graphene, the graphene wouldn't\nbreak."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169900,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course the pencil would."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172230,
    "dDurationMs": 7759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For their discovery, Geim and Novoselov were\nawarded the Nobel Prize for physics in 2010."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179989,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is only the beginning for Graphene."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182319,
    "dDurationMs": 6221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists are hard at work exploiting its\nunique properties to create thin, transparent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188540,
    "dDurationMs": 7089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flexible touch screens,\nSmaller, faster, more energy efficient computers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195629,
    "dDurationMs": 6381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tough composite materials\nAnd more efficient solar cells"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202010,
    "dDurationMs": 6369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now consider this is only one aspect of\nnanotechnology, so in order to think big you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208379,
    "dDurationMs": 2181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "need first consider the very small."
    } ]
  } ]
}
